From: Harvi654 <202698022+Harvi654@users.noreply.github.com>
Subject: [PATCH] iphlpapi: Keep an empty DNS server list when there is no server of the family.

AI-assisted (Claude), original code; LGPL-2.1-or-later. Not submitted
upstream.

Windows 10 returns the adapters from GetAdaptersAddresses(AF_INET6, 0)
with an empty FirstDnsServerAddress where there is no IPv6 DNS server
(measured, docs/wine-repro/iphlpapi-adapters). Wine asked dnsapi for the
servers of the requested family and returned its error for the whole
call, so on a Linux host whose resolver lists only IPv4 servers every
GetAdaptersAddresses(AF_INET6, ...) without GAA_FLAG_SKIP_DNS_SERVER
failed with DNS_ERROR_NO_DNS_SERVERS. CodeMeter's service (ABB
RobotStudio) makes that call at its start and then lists no local
address.

dns_info_alloc() now treats DNS_ERROR_NO_DNS_SERVERS as an empty list;
other errors still fail the call as before.

--- a/dlls/iphlpapi/iphlpapi_main.c
+++ b/dlls/iphlpapi/iphlpapi_main.c
@@ -1199,7 +1199,9 @@ static DWORD dns_info_alloc( IP_ADAPTER_ADDRESSES *aa, ULONG family, ULONG flags
                     break;
                 }
             }
-            if (!err)
+            /* no DNS server of this family: the adapter's list stays empty */
+            if (err == DNS_ERROR_NO_DNS_SERVERS) err = ERROR_SUCCESS;
+            else if (!err)
             {
                 next = &aa->FirstDnsServerAddress;
                 for (i = 0; i < servers->AddrCount; i++)
